---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import "../styles/pages.css";
---

<SiteLayout title="Terms and Conditions | CRE Alexa" description="Terms and conditions of attendance and participation for CRE events.">
  <article class="legal" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="kicker"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Terms and conditions</p>
      <h1 id="terms-title">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p>Terms and Conditions of Attendance and Participation for CRE Events</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <p class="legal-lead">By registering for or attending the Event, you agree that you have read, understood, and acknowledge and agree to the terms outlined in this Agreement.</p>

      <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#terms-1">Terms and Conditions of Attendance and Participation</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-2">Attendee Requirements</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-3">Conduct of Attendees</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-4">Fees; Refund</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-5">Intellectual Property</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-6">Disclaimer of Warranties; Limitation of Liability</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-7">Indemnity, Release, and Waiver</a></li>
          <li><a href="#terms-8">Miscellaneous</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <section id="terms-1">
        <h2>1. Terms and Conditions of Attendance and Participation</h2>
        <p>Reflected herein are the terms and conditions (the “Agreement”) governing your attendance at and participation in any CRE operated or sponsored event (the “Event”). By registering for or attending the Event, you agree to these terms and conditions, which form a binding legal contract between CRE (“CRE”) and the registered attendee or participant (“you” or “your”).</p>
        <p>If you are registering on behalf of another individual, it is your responsibility to ensure the person attending is aware of these terms and conditions and agrees to abide by them. By completing the registration on behalf of another individual, you represent and warrant that you have made the attendee or participant aware of these terms and that they have accepted them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-2">
        <h2>2. Attendee Requirements</h2>
        <h3>2.1 Purpose</h3>
        <p>CRE and its events are intended for professional networking purposes. CRE is designed to provide participants with opportunities to connect, collaborate, and engage in business-related discussions. The primary purpose of the Event is to foster professional relationships and promote industry growth.</p>
        <p>Actions inconsistent with this purpose may result in removal from the Event and potential restriction from future events at CRE’s sole and absolute discretion.</p>

        <h3>2.2 Admittance; Expenses</h3>
        <p>Your registration entitles you to admittance to the Event for which you have registered. Any and all other costs associated with your attendance shall be borne solely by you, and CRE shall have no liability for such costs.</p>
        <p>The Event may include sponsored or compensated food, beverages (both non-alcoholic and alcoholic), and other items, which may be provided on a discretionary basis.</p>

        <h3>2.3 Use of Likeness</h3>
        <p>By attending the Event, you grant CRE, together with its organizers, employees, agents, and representatives, the right to record, film, photograph, or otherwise capture your likeness in any media now available or later developed, and to distribute, broadcast, use, or otherwise globally disseminate such media in perpetuity without further approval from you or compensation to you.</p>
        <p>This includes, but is not limited to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The right to edit such media</li>
          <li>The right to use the media alone or with other information</li>
          <li>The right to allow others to use or disseminate the media</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.4 Event Content</h3>
        <p>You acknowledge and agree that CRE reserves the right to change any aspect of the Event, including but not limited to:</p>
        <ul class="legal-columns">
          <li>Event name</li>
          <li>Concessions served</li>
          <li>Themes</li>
          <li>Content</li>
          <li>Program</li>
          <li>Speakers</li>
          <li>Performers</li>
          <li>Hosts</li>
          <li>Moderators</li>
          <li>Venue</li>
          <li>Date and time</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-3">
        <h2>3. Conduct of Attendees</h2>
        <h3>3.1 Responsible Consumption</h3>
        <p>Alcohol may be served at the Event. You agree to consume responsibly. You are solely responsible for your actions and should refrain from behavior influenced by excessive alcohol consumption.</p>

        <h3>3.2 Professional Conduct</h3>
        <p>Participants are expected to conduct themselves professionally at all times. Disrespectful, offensive, or inappropriate behavior will not be tolerated, including but not limited to harassment, discrimination, or conduct that causes discomfort or harm to others.</p>

        <h3>3.3 Disruptive Conduct</h3>
        <p>CRE reserves the right to remove any attendee whose behavior is disruptive, hinders the Event, interferes with other attendees’ enjoyment, or is otherwise deemed inappropriate at CRE’s sole discretion.</p>

        <h3>3.4 Discretion of CRE</h3>
        <p>CRE reserves sole discretion in determining who may attend the Event. CRE may deny admission or remove any participant whose conduct violates this Agreement, poses a safety risk, or is deemed grounds for removal.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-4">
        <h2>4. Fees; Refund</h2>
        <h3>4.1 Payment</h3>
        <p>Payment is due upon registration. If payment is insufficient or declined, CRE may refuse admission without liability.</p>

        <h3>4.2 Taxes</h3>
        <p>Fees may be subject to applicable sales tax or other taxes, which will be charged in addition to the registration fee where required.</p>

        <h3>4.3 Refunds</h3>
        <p>If CRE elects to cancel, suspend, or reschedule the Event, CRE may, in its sole discretion, refund applicable fees.</p>
        <p>If the registration fee does not exceed Thirty and 00/100 Dollars ($30.00), CRE may, at its discretion, allow the fee to be applied to a future event.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-5">
        <h2>5. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>All intellectual property rights in and to the Event, Event content, and materials distributed at or in connection with the Event are owned by CRE or the Event sponsors or speakers.</p>
        <p>You may not reproduce, use, or distribute any trademarks or materials without prior written consent from CRE or the respective owner.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-6">
        <h2>6. Disclaimer of Warranties; Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>CRE makes no warranties regarding any aspect of the Event and expressly disclaims all implied warranties, including but not limited to fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, timeliness, and merchantability.</p>
        <p>The Event is provided on an “as-is” basis.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-7">
        <h2>7. Indemnity, Release, and Waiver</h2>
        <p>By attending the Event, you agree to indemnify and hold harmless CRE, its organizers, employees, agents, and representatives from any liability for injury, damage, or loss arising out of your participation.</p>
        <p>You assume all risks associated with attending the Event. CRE is not responsible for personal belongings or injuries arising from the Event.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms-8">
        <h2>8. Miscellaneous</h2>
        <p>Failure by CRE to exercise any right under this Agreement shall not constitute a waiver.</p>
        <p>CRE shall not be liable for failure to perform due to causes beyond its reasonable control.</p>
        <p>If any provision is found unenforceable, it shall be limited to the minimum extent necessary, and the remainder of the Agreement shall remain in effect.</p>
        <p>This Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the State of Texas. The parties agree to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts located in Travis County, Texas.</p>
        <p>The prevailing party in any action brought under this Agreement shall be entitled to recover reasonable attorneys’ fees and costs.</p>
        <p>This Agreement constitutes the complete and exclusive understanding between the parties and supersedes all prior agreements. No modification shall be valid unless in writing and signed by both parties.</p>
        <p>No agency, partnership, joint venture, or employment relationship is created by this Agreement.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
